{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"THEOplayerAdapter","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wraps a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"THEOplayer"},{"type":"text","text":" the integrator owns (created by the application or by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"react-native-theoplayer"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"THEOplayerRCTView"},{"type":"text","text":"); the adapter never owns or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destroys the host player — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"destroy()"},{"type":"text","text":" only detaches its listeners."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"THEOplayer’s API is main-thread affine while the SDK’s scheduler reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"playback state from its own native queues, so the adapter mirrors the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Android pattern: playback state is served from a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"snapshot"}]},{"type":"text","text":" refreshed on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the main thread (player events plus a periodic refresh timer), and every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"player command hops to the main queue. Timed metadata (ID3 \/ emsg \/"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"EXT-X-DATERANGE) is forwarded from THEOplayer’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"metadata"},{"type":"text","text":" text tracks as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"portable "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimedMetadataCue"},{"type":"text","tex